Talkiie bundled bopomofo data (Bopomofo/chars.txt, Bopomofo/words.txt)

Derived from McBopomofo (https://github.com/openvanilla/McBopomofo), tag 3.1.1,
commit f5ba010ce8795d283ee336ca7d16380f200bd2ec. Modifications:
  - chars.txt: single-character readings taken from Source/Data/BPMFBase.txt
    (bopomofo column only; characters outside the Big5/CNS sets are kept only
    when a word in words.txt uses them).
  - words.txt: 2-4 character words taken from Source/Data/phrase.occ and
    Source/Data/BPMFMappings.txt (NFC-normalized, CJK-only; no counts, no readings).
Generated by tools/lexicon/bopomofo-subset/build.sh in the Talkiie repository.

McBopomofo states that BPMFMappings.txt was "Originally simplified from tsi.src
of libtabe (BSD Licensed) with modifications", so the libtabe notices are
reproduced below as well. The names of the TaBE Project, the Computer Systems
and Communication Lab (Academia Sinica) and their contributors are not used to
endorse or promote this product.

